WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:03.949
Good morning, John; it is Monday. Your "Thoughts
from Places" video on Friday was absolutely

00:00:03.949 --> 00:00:07.970
amazing. Thank you very much for that. Nerdfighters,
if you did not watch that video either because

00:00:07.970 --> 00:00:11.510
you were, uh, away from your subscription
box, or because you did not want to click

00:00:11.510 --> 00:00:16.250
on the tombstone of Valva Couch, here is your
opportunity to click on the tombstone of Valva

00:00:16.250 --> 00:00:19.390
Couch and that will take you to John's "Thoughts
from Places" video. At the end of that video,

00:00:19.390 --> 00:00:21.900
there will be a link back to this video, and
you will get to watch it.

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:24.599
So, John, it occurred to me a little while
ago that you and I are a little bit like the

00:00:24.599 --> 00:00:28.749
presidents of Nerdfighteria; possibly, the
enlightened despots. But then, for several

00:00:28.749 --> 00:00:31.570
reasons, that analogy broke down. Because
it's not really a country-sized place, if

00:00:31.570 --> 00:00:34.430
you can call this place that isn't a place
"a place," and nerdfighters already have their

00:00:34.430 --> 00:00:38.240
own national governments, so it's more like
a town or a small city, and so, thus, we are

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:42.570
more like co-mayors. And so I wanted to talk
to a mayor about what being a mayor is like,

00:00:42.570 --> 00:00:43.570
and so I did this...

00:00:43.570 --> 00:00:44.630
[to John Engen] Good morning, John!

00:00:44.630 --> 00:00:45.820
&gt;&gt;JOHN ENGEN: [chuckles] Good morning, Hank.

00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:49.650
&gt;&gt;HANK: [chuckles] This is Missoula's mayor,
John Engen, and I had a chance to talk to

00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:53.170
him, and I feel like if you have a chance
to talk to your mayor, you should talk to

00:00:53.170 --> 00:00:54.170
your mayor.

00:00:54.170 --> 00:00:56.180
&gt;&gt;ENGEN: Generally speaking, everyone should
have a chance to talk to their mayor.

00:00:56.180 --> 00:00:57.791
&gt;&gt;HANK: But you've never lived in a very large
town.

00:00:57.791 --> 00:00:58.800
&gt;&gt;ENGEN: I have not.

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:02.090
Local government's kind of the front line.
This is your opportunity, really, to interact.

00:01:02.090 --> 00:01:03.630
&gt;&gt;HANK: So I'm wanna ask you a couple, uh,
hard-hitting questions...

00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:04.630
&gt;&gt;ENGEN: Yes.

00:01:04.630 --> 00:01:05.640
&gt;&gt;HANK: ...um, below the belt.

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:06.640
&gt;&gt;ENGEN: 'Kay.

00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:07.640
&gt;&gt;HANK: Do you have any pets?

00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:12.749
&gt;&gt;ENGEN: We have a rescued labradoodle named
Odie, uh, we have a Humane Society cat named

00:01:12.749 --> 00:01:19.780
Moose, and uh, we just lost our 13-year-old
greyhound, my beloved Patches.

00:01:19.780 --> 00:01:20.780
&gt;&gt;HANK: Oh. I have a greyhound.

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:21.780
&gt;&gt;ENGEN: Do you?

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:22.780
&gt;&gt;HANK: Yeah.

00:01:22.780 --> 00:01:23.780
&gt;&gt;ENGEN: Yeah, they're fantastic dogs.

00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:24.780
&gt;&gt;HANK: She's a sweetie; she's pathetic.

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:28.251
&gt;&gt;ENGEN: Yeah. Patches was what we call "food-focused,"
which is really unusual in our family.

00:01:28.251 --> 00:01:29.251
&gt;&gt;HANK: [laughs]

00:01:29.251 --> 00:01:31.429
What did you do before you were mayor? Jobs?

00:01:31.429 --> 00:01:33.039
&gt;&gt;ENGEN: Golf Land, which was...

00:01:33.039 --> 00:01:34.100
&gt;&gt;HANK: Golf Land!

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:35.329
&gt;&gt;ENGEN: ...an indoor miniature golf course...

00:01:35.329 --> 00:01:36.380
&gt;&gt;HANK: And that's here. That was here.

00:01:36.380 --> 00:01:37.380
&gt;&gt;ENGEN: It was.

00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:38.380
&gt;&gt;HANK: We lost Golf Land!

00:01:38.380 --> 00:01:39.499
&gt;&gt;ENGEN: Yeah, quite some time ago.

00:01:39.499 --> 00:01:43.859
&gt;&gt;HANK: Ugh. We just lost Qwivals, too. I
feel like we're lacking for family fun centers.

00:01:43.859 --> 00:01:46.322
&gt;&gt;ENGEN: I didn't know that was a... that's
the maze... corn maze?

00:01:46.322 --> 00:01:47.859
&gt;&gt;HANK: Go Karts, corn maze,...

00:01:47.859 --> 00:01:48.859
&gt;&gt;ENGEN: Yeah?

00:01:48.859 --> 00:01:49.859
&gt;&gt;HANK: ...arcade games,...

00:01:49.859 --> 00:01:51.219
&gt;&gt;ENGEN: Generally, I don't like to be...

00:01:51.219 --> 00:01:52.219
&gt;&gt;HANK: ...bouncy castles!

00:01:52.219 --> 00:01:54.789
&gt;&gt;ENGEN: ...around that much... corn, and
I'm not allowed in bouncy things, so....

00:01:54.789 --> 00:01:55.789
&gt;&gt;HANK: [laughs]

00:01:55.789 --> 00:01:57.189
&gt;&gt;ENGEN: ...there's a restraining order.

00:01:57.189 --> 00:02:01.640
Golf Land, Hansen's Famous Ice Cream Store,
and then I worked for the local newspaper;

00:02:01.640 --> 00:02:02.860
I worked for the Missoulian for a long time...

00:02:02.860 --> 00:02:04.899
&gt;&gt;HANK: How does mayoring compare with all
of your other jobs?

00:02:04.899 --> 00:02:09.200
&gt;&gt;ENGEN: Best job I've ever had, love the
job, uh, very challenging,...

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:10.200
&gt;&gt;HANK: Yeah.

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:15.400
&gt;&gt;ENGEN: ...just, uh, a fantastic education,
a real opportunity to... to get things done.

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:18.239
&gt;&gt;HANK: As a mayor, what do you actually do?

00:02:18.239 --> 00:02:19.239
&gt;&gt;ENGEN: Oh.

00:02:19.239 --> 00:02:21.460
&gt;&gt;HANK: Just this? This is what you do? You
talk to people on couches?

00:02:21.460 --> 00:02:23.550
&gt;&gt;ENGEN: I didn't think we'd get to that question,
uh...

00:02:23.550 --> 00:02:24.550
&gt;&gt;HANK: [laughs]

00:02:24.550 --> 00:02:27.879
&gt;&gt;ENGEN: I am responsible for the day-to-day
operations of the city of Missoula. We have

00:02:27.879 --> 00:02:30.209
about 500 full-time employees.

00:02:30.209 --> 00:02:34.730
&gt;&gt;HANK: You're basically the chief executive
of a 500-person corporation that runs a city.

00:02:34.730 --> 00:02:38.750
&gt;&gt;ENGEN: ...which I try not to think about
too much, because it scares me. I know, right?

00:02:38.750 --> 00:02:39.750
&gt;&gt;HANK: [chuckles]

00:02:39.750 --> 00:02:40.750
&gt;&gt;ENGEN: Really.

00:02:40.750 --> 00:02:41.750
Uh, I get my own firetruck.

00:02:41.750 --> 00:02:43.319
&gt;&gt;HANK: Oh, I didn't know that.

00:02:43.319 --> 00:02:44.319
&gt;&gt;ENGEN: Few people do.

00:02:44.319 --> 00:02:45.360
&gt;&gt;HANK: Can you loan it out?

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:46.360
&gt;&gt;ENGEN: Oh, sure.

00:02:46.360 --> 00:02:47.360
&gt;&gt;HANK: [chuckling] Great....

00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:49.190
&gt;&gt;ENGEN: We do a lot... prom night, in particular.

00:02:49.190 --> 00:02:50.629
&gt;&gt;HANK: Probably your primary income source.

00:02:50.629 --> 00:02:51.629
&gt;&gt;ENGEN: [laughing] Yeah.

00:02:51.629 --> 00:02:52.629
&gt;&gt;HANK: Firetruck rental! [laughs]

00:02:52.629 --> 00:02:55.420
&gt;&gt;ENGEN: Yes. It's all about new revenue schemes.

00:02:55.420 --> 00:02:58.530
&gt;&gt;HANK: [laughs] I mean, most of the time,
they're just sitting there!

00:02:58.530 --> 00:03:02.959
&gt;&gt;ENGEN: And there's noth... there's nothing
like a ladder truck on an April evening, Lady

00:03:02.959 --> 00:03:04.110
Gaga in the background.

00:03:04.110 --> 00:03:05.110
&gt;&gt;HANK: Oh, man.

00:03:05.110 --> 00:03:06.110
&gt;&gt;ENGEN: Yeah.

00:03:06.110 --> 00:03:07.260
&gt;&gt;HANK: My wife is... would love me forever.

00:03:07.260 --> 00:03:08.260
&gt;&gt;ENGEN: Yeah?

00:03:08.260 --> 00:03:09.260
&gt;&gt;HANK: No she wouldn't; she hates heights.

00:03:09.260 --> 00:03:10.260
&gt;&gt;ENGEN: [chuckles]

00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:12.439
&gt;&gt;HANK [to camera]: I didn't get the end part
where we shook hands and I said, "Thank you,

00:03:12.439 --> 00:03:15.349
Mayor Engen," because my camera ran out of
card space.

00:03:15.349 --> 00:03:18.849
I had a great time talking to him; if you
live in Missoula, you should vote for him.

00:03:18.849 --> 00:03:23.719
And again, are you a Seattleite or a Portlander?
I'm going to be in your city, playing music

00:03:23.719 --> 00:03:28.050
with funny people like Mike Furman and Paul
and Storm at the end of March. It's going

00:03:28.050 --> 00:03:31.359
to be fun; tickets are $20 each and they're
selling out fast.

00:03:31.359 --> 00:03:36.400
And finally, Nerdfighteria: Sincere apologies
for never letting you challenge us to do something

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:40.609
in return for you figuring out the space pasta
mess. Please leave us challenges in the comments;

00:03:40.609 --> 00:03:45.829
they can be things like, "Interview your mayor,"
which... I wish somebody had challenged me

00:03:45.829 --> 00:03:48.299
to do that, because I just did it. Gah!

00:03:48.299 --> 00:03:51.579
That is all. I need to go eat Chinese food.
John, I'll see you on Wednesday.

00:03:51.579 --> 00:03:52.579
&gt;&gt;[Music from DR NOISE'S "Crazy Town"]: ...a
twisted little place called Crazy Town, where

00:03:52.579 --> 00:03:52.588
a horse is the mayor of all of us...

